note <Functional tests for the text module. `want hold` asserts the body is true, `want miss` asserts it is false. The predicate (is-equal, contains, starts-with) is the call inside.>

load @cluesurf/base/code/text
  find to-upper-case
  find trim
  find contains
  find starts-with

test <trim then uppercase yields a clean token>
  want hold
    call is-equal
      call to-upper-case
        call trim
          text <  hello  >
      text <HELLO>

test <contains finds a present substring>
  want hold
    call contains
      text <hello world>
      text <world>

test <contains rejects an absent substring>
  want miss
    call contains
      text <hello world>
      text <absent>

test <starts-with matches a prefix>
  want hold
    call starts-with
      text <hello world>
      text <hello>
